<p>Palma de Mallorca Airport (PMI), also known as Son Sant Joan Airport, lies around 8 kilometres east of Palma city and is Spain's third-busiest airport, a status that reflects Mallorca's position as one of the country's most visited holiday destinations. Flights land here year-round, though the volume rises sharply through the summer months, which is when pre-booking a transfer for a longer, hillside journey like this one is especially worthwhile.</p>
